<title>UK: Toyota unit sets C$125 million six-year bond.</title>
<headline>Toyota unit sets C$125 million six-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The following bond was announced by joint lead managers CIBC Wood Gundy and Paribas Capital Markets.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TOYOTA CREDIT CANADA INC</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  TOYOTA MOTOR FINANCE NETERLANDS BV</p>
<p> AMT    C$125 MLN     COUPON     5.25	MATURITY    31.DEC.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.75    PAY DATE  S 06.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.15     SPREAD	+30 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/CA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.275     SELL CONC  1.60	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.0 PCT 2001 CANADA GOVERNMENT BOND</p>
<p> NOTES	SENIR, UNSECURED ND UNSUBORDINATED.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
